[36m(TaskRunner pid=1955391)[0m     "snippet": "---\ntitle: Who Remembers These 40 Short-Lived FOX TV Shows [VIDEO]\nauthor: Blexmedia\ndate: 2024-09-21\n---\nFOX has long been a network known for its vast programming. However, beneath the surface of the long-running hits lies a treasure trove of short-lived series that, despite their brief runs, left an indelible mark on the television landscape.\n\nREAD: Who Remembers These 15 Short-Lived UPN TV Shows [VIDEO]\n\nThese shows, often overshadowed by their more enduring counterparts, offered unique storylines, memorable characters, and sometimes even cult followings. From dramas to sitcoms and everything in between, FOX's short-lived series showcased a diverse range of programming.\n\nLet's embark on a journey down memory lane and revisit some of these forgotten gems. Some may be familiar to longtime fans, while others might be completely new to you. Join us as we explore the intriguing world of FOX's short-lived television shows.\n\nSouth Central\n\nLasted: 1 season, 10 episodes\n\nStarring Tina Lifford, Larenz Tate, Tasha Scott, Keith Mbulo, Paula Kelly and Ken Page, its gritty drama about life in South Los Angeles, focusing on a single mother of three raising her children amid challenges like gang violence and poverty.\n\nM.A.N.T.I.S.\n\nLasted: 1 season, 22 episodes\n\nsuperhero TV series about Dr. Miles Hawkins, a paralyzed scientist who creates an exoskeleton that allows him to walk and gives him superhuman abilities. He becomes the crime-fighting M.A.N.T.I.S. (Mechanically Augmented Neuro Transmitter Interception System) to seek justice.\n\n413 Hope St\n\nLasted: 1 season, 10 episodes\n\nStarring Richard Roundtree, Jesse L. Martin, Shari Headley, and more, the show is set in a community crisis center. Founded by Phil (Roundtree), a successful corporate executive, the center was established in the building where his teenage son was tragically gunned down after refusing to give up his sneakers to a street thug.\n\nThis drama explores the social issues affecting inner-city youth, including addiction and teen pregnancy.\"\n\nLawless\n\nLasted: 1 season, 6 episodes (5 unaired)\n\nThe show stars former NFL player Brian Bosworth as John Lawless, an ex-special forces operative who becomes a motorcycle-riding private investigator in Miami's South Beach"
